
This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html

Fixed VAD regression (from Projects):
  g++ -std=c++11 -Wall -Wextra -I C3_KEYWORD/test/vad/mocks -I C3_KEYWORD/include C3_KEYWORD/test/vad/test_fixed.cpp C3_KEYWORD/src/audio_detector.cpp -o /tmp/keyword-vad-fixed
  /tmp/keyword-vad-fixed

Checks silence, exact onset threshold, minimum onset, hysteresis, quiet duration,
window completion, startup spikes and threshold preservation after stream reset.

Per-keyword confidence regression (from Projects):
  g++ -std=c++11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -I C3_KEYWORD/test/event_mapper -I C3_KEYWORD/include C3_KEYWORD/test/event_mapper/test_thresholds.cpp C3_KEYWORD/src/event_mapper.cpp -o /tmp/keyword-thresholds
  /tmp/keyword-thresholds

Checks each configured rule at its exact threshold, just below it, at full
confidence and with failed inference; rejects noise and unmapped labels.

PIUU v1 pristine/optimized MFCC parity (from C3_KEYWORD; g++ required):
  python3 -B tests/verify_mfcc_export.py '../piuu-cpp-mcu-v1-impulse-#1' --audio model-backups/audio-antes-oct4/real_audio.pcm --output reports/piuu-v1-mfcc-parity.json

Compares 40 windows (8 synthetic + 32 existing historical PCM windows), including
repeated extraction to exercise caches. Uses pristine exported MFCC parameters;
fails for nonfinite features or maximum absolute difference >= 1e-5.
This checks features on the host, not acoustic accuracy or ESP32 latency.
